{"_id":"697d3e3f19b7a824528a467c","nodeId":"xgJCbwDNWPbYV2bCILRo0","roadmapSlug":"ruby-on-rails","createdAt":"2026-01-30T23:26:55.240Z","description":"# Callbacks\n\nCallbacks are methods that get called at certain moments in the lifecycle of an Active Record object. These moments can include creation, updating, deletion, validation, or saving. By using callbacks, you can trigger logic before or after these actions, allowing you to perform tasks like data validation, auditing, or related object updates automatically","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Active Record Callbacks","url":"https://guides.rubyonrails.org/active_record_callbacks.html","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a282"},{"type":"article","title":"Active Record Callbacks | The Odin Project","url":"https://www.theodinproject.com/lessons/ruby-on-rails-active-record-callbacks","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a283"},{"type":"article","title":"Rails ActiveRecord Callbacks ΓÇö cheatsheet & best practices","url":"https://medium.com/@jaysadiq/rails-activerecord-callbacks-cheatsheet-55fdb37f76ef","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a284"},{"type":"article","title":"Ruby on Rails ActiveRecord Callbacks","url":"https://dev.to/eapenzac/ruby-on-rails-activerecord-callbacks-597a","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a285"},{"type":"video","title":"Understanding Active Record Callbacks","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-31AlGv96Y","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a286"},{"type":"video","title":"Callbacks","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GLBMfB8N1G8","_id":"697d3e3f5c049b276520a287"}],"updatedAt":"2026-01-30T23:26:55.240Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ruby-on-rails/content/xgJCbwDNWPbYV2bCILRo0.md"}